WEBVTT

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.320
Hey, Natsumi. You're gonna 
be late for school.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.150
You still haven't changed?

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.530
Yeah, I'm going to now.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.190
What's that you're holding?

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.880
A toy fortune dispenser I 
got at the candy store.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.980
Want me to read your fortune, too?

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.000
You don't have to do that...

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.050
Fortunes
Beware of water - Bad Luck

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.960
Let's see...

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.140
Yikes, bad luck.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.210
It says to beware of water.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.380
You'd better be careful today, Nee-chan.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.620
A-As if a toy fortune like that 
would actually come true.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.040
Forget about that. Just get ready.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.890
You're actually kinda worried 
though, aren't you?

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.570
I am not!

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.750
It's not supposed to rain today,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.150
and I won't even be near any water.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:58.570
Okay, we're all going 
to clean the pool today.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.360
The pool! Sweet!

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.080
Oh! The pool?!

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.950
The pool!

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.950
I'll clean it!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.460
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.460
<b>We Ate Okonomiyaki</b>

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.460
Ren-chon, it's your first time 
seeing the school pool, isn't it?!

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.780
Yes, it is!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.740
Hey, no running. You'll slip.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.580
Why do we have to clean 
the pool, of all things?

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.730
Is something wrong?

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:15.040
Well, Natsumi gave me a fortune 
that said "beware of water."

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.560
Not that I believe in fortunes,

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.430
but there's nothing wrong 
with being careful.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.970
Outta the way!

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.010
I can't stop!

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.520
Whew, that was close.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.270
Senpai! Are you okay?!

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.810
Man, I'd be soaked now if 
you hadn't been there.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.020
Thanks, Nee-chan.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.910
<i>I</i> fell! <i>I'm</i> soaked!

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.190
Don't thank me! Apologize!

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.980
You did that on purpose to make me 
scared of that fortune, didn't you?!

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.690
It wasn't on purpose.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.160
I totally forgot about that fortune, anyway.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.870
Hotaru, forget about the pool. 
Let's clean the outside instead.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:52.900
That fortune scares me!

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.580
Huh? I thought you didn't 
believe in fortunes...

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.050
I don't, but they scare me!

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.140
Wow, it's really dirty here.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.200
Cool! I'll try another one!

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.480
Oh, this detergent cleans 
it off pretty well.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.440
Okay, now to get the rest!

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.720
Hey. Getting it all clean?

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.490
Yes, but that handle won't turn.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.080
It hasn't been used in a 
year. Maybe it's rusted.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.700
Why don't we try turning it together?

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.050
Will you get that side?

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.080
Okay.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.670
And that's clean, too.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.040
Now to work on something else.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.610
One, two...

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.720
That's cold!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.720
Cold! Cold! Cold!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.630
Whoa, Koma-chan, you were here?

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.810
S-Sorry!

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.350
Wh-Why am I getting into 
so many water disasters?

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:00.530
Let's quit cleaning here and 
go somewhere with less water.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:04.570
S-Sure... I think that's for the best, too.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.770
So, um, where should we go clean next?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.670
I have a bad feeling. We should be careful.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.710
Huh? Okay...

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.790
Hey, Nii-chan, help me out.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.340
I can't do this on my own.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.690
Watch it!

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.020
Darn it, Onii-chan, be careful with that!

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.100
You almost got water on me again!

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.360
Jeez. Good thing I was paying attention.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:37.450
But now we know you can avoid 
bad fortunes if you try, huh?

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:41.220
That's right. Well, ready to start cleaning?

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.940
Yeah, oka—

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.650
I'll cover this side, too.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.770
My eyes! Something's shooting my eyes!

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.220
It's the curse of the fortune!

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.770
Senpai, calm down!

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.830
It's not a curse! It's water!

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.190
Sorry, Koma-chan.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.660
I guess the fortune came true.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.260
I guess you couldn't deny fate, after all.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:08.910
Okay, good work today, everyone.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.130
Question! Can we start 
using the pool tomorrow?

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.340
Tomorrow's the school's anniversary,

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.350
so we'll open the pool the day after that.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.010
The school's anniversary?

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.600
Oh, yeah! We get the day off tomorrow!

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.930
On that note, we're all done cleaning.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.860
Back to class, everyone.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.590
Finally, that's over.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:31.760
It really has been rough on you.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.740
Hey, don't get so down.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.700
Be glad you got to enjoy 
the pool a little early.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:39.580
Senpai!

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.310
Whew, it's nice and cool!

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.930
This feels great!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.010
Huh? It feels good?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.590
I wanna do that, too!

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:56.710
Hmm...

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.350
All right. You all worked hard today,

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.460
so as a special treat, 
you can get in the pool.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.020
Yay!

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.050
Uh, but I don't have a change of clothes...

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:09.680
Don't worry. There are extra 
underclothes in the faculty room.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.610
Really? Okay, then!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.160
Here I go!

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.970
They have so much energy.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:39.680
Sure is nice to be young.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:44.770
Wait. Are there enough extra 
underclothes for all of them?

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.290
Oh, well. They'll dry off fast.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.520
Nee-chan...

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.810
Huh?

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:29.860
What do you, like, think about this?

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:30.820
About what?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:35.880
I mean, getting a day off during the 
week is a special thing, right?

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:42.000
It's, like, different 
from other days, you know?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.090
Well, it's the anniversary 
of the school's founding.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:50.520
But right now, it's no different 
from a normal Sunday.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.560
Isn't it going to waste if 
we don't do something fun?

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.340
Huh? I don't want to do anything. It's too hot.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.970
I know. I'll read your fortune for today.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.350
Let's see...

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.490
Hey! Don't start that again!

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:05.520
Oh, look at this, Nee-chan.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.520
Bad luck again?!

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:11.550
"Wise to go out. Unwise to stay in."

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.650
Does that mean something bad will 
happen if I stay in the house?

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.690
Now we have no choice but to go outside!

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.260
It was right about the water yesterday!

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.620
Huh?

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:23.390
<i>Hello, Hotarun?</i>

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:26.080
<i>We're going out. Want to tag along?</i>

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:30.780
Sorry, I have to stay at home today.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.050
My mom's not home, and we 
have a delivery coming.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.510
Oh, okay.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.540
No problem. See you later.

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.510
Hotaru can't make it?

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.130
She said she has to stay at home.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:45.890
Okay, so next is...

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:55.530
I bet Senpai and the others are 
out playing together right now...

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.980
This is it! This is the way to go!

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:36.760
Time moves so slowly when you're 
by yourself on a weekday...

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.560
I ended up outside anyway.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:41.490
Nattsun, what are we doing?

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.680
I haven't decided, but we're gonna 
go somewhere and do something.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.490
You never think anything through.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:53.900
It feels weird to be out walking 
around on a weekday, huh?

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:57.330
Yeah. We'd normally be in school right now.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:00.420
If the police found us, 
maybe we'd get arrested.

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:01.550
Arrested!

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.720
Don't say things like that.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:22.130
Whew, I got pretty worried there.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.550
I got nervous, even though we 
didn't do anything wrong!

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:26.320
The school's anniversary is intense!

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.060
You freaked out a little, 
didn't you, Nee-chan?

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:29.470
I-I did no—

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:35.180
Freaked out?

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.300
I did not!

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.950
Pechi, want to play here?

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:45.160
Pechi?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.310
I hope that delivery comes soon...

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.330
With the start of summer this week,

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:59.150
<b>Beach Season
Opens</b>

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:59.150
<b>Special</b>

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:59.150
<b>Beach Season Begins Around the Country</b>

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:59.940
the excited voices of children can 
be heard on beaches all over—

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:06.960
I wonder what the others 
are doing right now...

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:19.920
It's here!

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.010
Now I can play with everyone!

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:38.650
I didn't ask where they were going.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.490
Hotarun!

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.700
We came to visit.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.340
We thought you might be 
bored here all alone.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:53.870
Are you done watching the house?

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.210
Yeah!

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.570
This is pretty hard.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:01.320
You'll get better as you get used to it.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:05.760
Huh?

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.670
It's really coming down.

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.820
Doesn't look like it'll stop anytime soon.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:19.410
Koma-chan, are your disasters 
still happening?

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:23.960
What? But my fortune this morning 
said I should go out today...

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.530
Nee-chan! Hurry up!

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:41.770
We're already soaked. 
What difference does running make?

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:43.660
Man, that rain is nuts!

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:44.930
Hide out in the candy store!

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:47.900
What happened to you
guys? You're drenched.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.460
We were playing outside 
and it started raining...

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:52.000
All because you got that 
weird fortune, Nee-chan!

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.790
It's not my fault! It's the fortune's fault!

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.790
Candy Store! It's a whistle! A whistle!

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:59.100
It's a whistle! A whistle!

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:59.880
I can't understand if you all talk at once.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:04.630
Whew, my clothes are soaked, 
but thankfully there's a free shelter here.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.770
It's a whistle! It whistles!

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.940
Look, Candy Store! Candy Store!

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.320
What? Don't treat this as a free shelter!

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:08.760
Candy Store! Candy Store, it's a whistle!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:11.230
I told you, don't all talk at once!

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.720
Look, it's a whistle! Isn't it 
amazing?! It's amazing, right?!

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:18.430
Okay, look! I'll get you some clothes, 
so just go in back already!

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.610
There, all changed.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:32.090
Don't leave your wet clothes on the floor.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:35.520
I'm surprised you have clothes 
in all these different sizes.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:38.790
Yeah, my clothes from when 
I was a kid are still here.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:42.390
Oh, Hotaru-chan, I didn't know your size,

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.050
so I got you something I still use.

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:48.130
O-Oh... Really?

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.880
I can understand the "get rich 
quick" tracksuit, though.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.620
It's right in line with your interests.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.600
But...

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.070
Who knew you wore frilly stuff like 
that when you were in first grade?

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:02.560
Huh. Wow.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.660
Shut up! My parents bought it!

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:08.030
I wasn't into that stuff!

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.600
Why am I the only one in a costume?

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.840
My parents got that as 
a gift from somewhere,

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.890
when I was in fourth grade.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:18.040
Fourth grade?!

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:24.770
Anyway, shouldn't you guys be in school?

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:27.450
Today's the school's anniversary.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.380
The school's anniversary?

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.470
Oh, yeah, they had something like that.

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:34.220
Oh, it's three already?

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.260
Classes would normally be 
ending right about now.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.970
I guess that's the end of 
our time to feel special.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.670
To feel special?

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:47.440
Natsumi said today was a special 
day, so she wanted to do something.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.980
So we went outside, and then this happened.

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:54.460
Enough about that. I'm hungry.

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:56.990
That's right, we didn't eat lunch, did we?

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.960
Oh, you guys haven't eaten yet?

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:02.550
No, we've been out playing all day.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:06.380
Sheesh. You school kids sure have it easy.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.610
Okay, fine. I'll make you something.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.620
You're so nice!

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:15.180
Food!

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:21.140
I'll make okonomiyaki, 
so take this hot plate in.

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.420
Okay.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:25.270
There are paper plates in the 
bottom of the cupboard there.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:26.480
Grab those, too.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.480
Okay!

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:32.600
I've got pork, mochi, cheese, 
and shrimp. Which do you want?

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:35.030
All of them, of course!

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:38.020
You know, there's a little 
thing called "restraint."

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.280
We're having okonomiyaki!

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:45.790
That reminds me.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.390
I made a teru-teru bouzu mask the other day,

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:51.340
and Koma-chan didn't know what it was.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.050
Draws on anything!
Trick Ink

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:56.650
Oh, the thing that made Nee-chan cry?

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:57.380
Yeah.

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.180
I-I didn't cry!

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.630
Like this.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:03.320
I can totally tell it's Ren-chon.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.400
Why'd that make you cry, Nee-chan?

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:08.690
I couldn't tell because she was 
wearing a raincoat with it!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.060
Also, I wasn't crying!

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:14.280
I'm not sure I'd recognize that 
as a teru-teru bouzu, though.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.710
Huh? Really?

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.860
Yeah, I couldn't recognize it, either.

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:22.980
But if you had a raincoat 
on, it might look like one.

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:35.190
What's with the teru-teru bouzu mask?

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:37.470
It'll be ready soon. Just sit tight.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:41.980
That's one smug face.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:44.430
How did Candy Store figure 
it out from just the mask?

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:51.860
Okay, it's ready.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.330
Oh, here we go!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.920
So let's get cooking!

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.940
Hang on. Do you know how to cook these?

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.990
You cook it like anything else, 
right? What do you mean?

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:04.700
And that's exactly why I 
can't trust you with this.

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:07.270
Okay, as a special treat,

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:10.640
today I'm going to show you 
how to make good okonomiyaki.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:14.090
What, are you like the hotpot master, 
but an okonomiyaki master?

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:19.190
First, spread plenty of 
oil on the hot plate.

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:21.090
Pile it on good and thick.

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:23.620
You use lots of oil?

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.560
That makes it cook up nice and crispy.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:28.560
Then you fry the batter.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:34.600
Then, after you put on the 
meat and other toppings,

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.550
you make a little crater in the middle,

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:40.230
and pour broth over it.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:47.730
The broth that spills over 
the edges gets scorched,

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.310
so you pull the scorched 
parts back into the batter.

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:52.870
Okonomiyaki uses scorching, too?

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:55.250
Yeah, and it's really tasty.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:59.720
So, now we just flip it over, 
let it fry a bit, and...

00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:03.720
It's done!

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.760
My double-chopsticks are ready!

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.140
Let's eat!

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:12.290
Hang on. I haven't put the 
sauce on yet. Chill out.

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.070
Here.

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:28.870
All right, then...

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.080
Let's eat!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:36.070
Whoa! That's good!

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:39.460
It's crispy outside, 
but gooey inside, like takoyaki!

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:43.220
Isn't it? Better eat every 
bite with gratitude.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:44.820
It's delicious!

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:45.970
Yeah!

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:49.370
You've got sauce all over your face.

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:51.930
It's so good!

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:02.090
I'm stuffed. Thanks for the meal.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:05.130
Well? Did it feel like a special experience?

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:08.280
Totally! I couldn't be 
more satisfied, Senpai!

00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:11.890
Oh, it stopped raining.

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.080
Maybe Nee-chan's curse wore off.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.500
You're still saying that? It's not a curse!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.340
What's this about a curse?

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:21.710
Natsumi decided to read my fortune,

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.720
and I keep getting bad ones.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.880
It's the fortune dispenser 
I bought from here.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.470
Fortune dispenser? You mean...

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.750
This prank thing?

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:35.890
Prank
Bad Luck Fortunes
Gives "bad luck"
every time!

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.890
Yeah, that's it!

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:38.940
This was meant as a prank?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.680
You bought it. You're not 
supposed to forget that.

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.920
Whew, thank goodness, Nee-chan!

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:45.900
It's meant as a prank. 
They all say "bad luck!"

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:52.370
Oh, so all that stuff I went through 
wasn't actually disasters?

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:58.000
No...

00:21:58.740 --> 00:22:01.720
I'd say those were definitely disasters.

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:21.520
<b>That's all for today</b>

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:44.390
<i>The girl who fights for love 
and justice, Pretty Cute!</i>

00:23:44.390 --> 00:23:46.650
<i>Oh, how cute!</i>

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:48.330
<i>Gecko! Gecko! Gecko! Gecko!</i>

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:50.450
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:53.450
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:53.450
<b>We Made Friends with Fireflies</b>

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:55.990
